mer months the one Mac  that I think we could get revealed and  released is the Apple silicon Mac Pro  which has been delayed it didn't make  the two-year timeline when we were  expecting at the end of last year but I  think by the summer time we should see  it but unfortunately it looks like we're  no longer getting the M2 extreme chip  with four dies that's going to be  insanely powerful looks like we're not  getting that most likely it's gonna have  the M2 Ultra and that chip might be  exclusive to the Mac Pro only and not  coming to the Max studio just to make  the Mac Pro more special and then  finally in the fall I do believe we're  gonna get the M3 MacBook Air update and  that ship is going to be amazing because  it is going to be on three nanometer for  sure and that's going to greatly improve  the battery life and other than that I  don't think the design is going to  change because it just got refreshed and  redesigned but Apple might add in some  more features to make it a little bit  nicer and we also might get another 13  inch M3 MacBook Pro update or there is a  chance it could get canceled if we do  get that 15 inch MacBook Air now other  than that I do think we might get an  iMac Pro except I don't know when it  would get released but probably not and  we probably won't get a Mac Studio  update I don't think it's coming this  year and I don't think the 24 inch iMac  update is coming until  2024. so with that said let's go into  the iPad side of things for this year I  don't think we're going to get any iPads  at all until the fall because we just  got a bunch of updates between September  and October we're probably gonna get a  new iPad Air 6 and a very small iPad 11  budget iPad update probably just the  chip getting upgraded and that might be  all we might even get the iPad Mini 7  according to Ming shaquel it could come  as early as late 2023 but it could get  delayed until  2024 as well and I don't think we're  gonna get any iPad Pros until later